senses.gloss:
संलापकः A kind of minor drama,
said to be of a controversial kind;
see S. D. 549.

संख्यं War, battle, fight; संख्ये
द्विषां वीररसं चकार Vikr. 1. 68, 70;
Ve. 3. 25; Śi. 18. 70; Māl. 8. 9.

संतानकः One of the five trees of
Indra's paradise or its flower;
Ku. 6. 46, 7. 3; Śi. 6. 67.

संदंश् {c1c} P.
1 To bite, sting;
संदष्टाधरपल्लवा Amaru. 32.
--2 (a)
To stick or adhere closely to, cling;
उरसा संदष्टसर्पत्वचा Ś. 7. 11;
संदष्टवस्त्रेष्वबलानितंबेषु R. 16. 65, 48. (b)
To press together, crush by pressure;
संदष्टकुसुमशयनानि गात्राणि Ś. 3. 18.

संप्रसारणं The change of य्, व्, र्,
and ल् to इ, उ, ऋ, and ऌ respectively;
इग्यणः संप्रसारणं P. I. 1. 45.

संफेटः An angry or tumultuous
conflict, an incident describing the
mutual encounter of angry persons;
see S. D. 379, 420; e. g. the
encounter between माधा and अघोरघंट.
in Māl. act {5}

संमद a. Greatly delighted, happy,
--दः Great joy, delight, happiness;
Śi. 15. 77.

सांयात्रिकः A sea-trader, a
merchant trading by sea (पोतवणिक्);
Pt. 1. 316.

1 Vicinity, proximity;
वदनामलेंदुसांनिध्यतः Māl. 3. 5.
--2
Presence, attendance; R. 4. 6; 7. 3;
Ku. 7. 33.
